<title>POLAND: Poland sells PLN 674 mln bonds to public.</title>
<headline>Poland sells PLN 674 mln bonds to public.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish finance ministry sold 323 million zlotys ($92.7 million) of one-year bonds due on June 4, 1998 to the public until July 20, it said in a Wednesday statement.</p>
<p>It also sold 351 million zlotys of floating three-year bonds maturing on May 6, 2000 until the end of the public offer on July 20.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 ($ = 3.484 Polish Zlotys)</p>
</text>
